{"kind":"assert","text":"One quarter of request 450274ee conflicts with a ratified decision this repository already made, and I am not resolving that by myself.\n\nThe request asks me to update SECURITY.md to point reporters at GitHub private vulnerability reporting \"instead of an unspecified direct contact\". I made that change, and the full suite refused it:\n\n  public_surface_test.go:74: SECURITY.md does not contain required public surface \"Report vulnerabilities privately and directly to the maintainer\"\n  public_surface_test.go:89: SECURITY.md contains obsolete or personal disclosure channel \"security/advisories/new\"\n\nTestPublicRepositorySurface pins that exact sentence as required and that exact URL as forbidden. It is not an accident of wording. Commit 27ad16c2, \"Make private maintainer disclosure the public policy\", says it directly: README and SECURITY direct reports privately to the maintainer \"without publishing a personal address or mandating GitHub advisory settings\", and the regression exists to hold that.\n\nThe reasoning behind it is in SECURITY.md itself and I think it is sound: repository visibility and issue availability are GitHub settings outside this source tree, source CI cannot guarantee them, and the page says to recheck them before every public update. Documenting a route that depends on a setting the build cannot verify risks sending a reporter to a channel that is closed - and a vulnerability reporter who finds a dead private channel may well fall back to a public issue, which is the outcome both positions are trying to prevent.\n\nThe request asserts the setting is already enabled. That may be true. But \"enabled today\" and \"guaranteed by anything in this tree\" are different claims, and the second is what the existing policy turns on. I cannot verify a GitHub repository setting from here at all, so I would be substituting the request's assertion for a tested decision on no evidence of my own.\n\nSo I have reverted my SECURITY.md change and left that gate standing. Deleting another actor's ratified policy gate because a later request assumed otherwise is not mine to do, and doing it quietly inside a four-part change would be worse.\n\nThe other three parts have no conflict and are done: CI now runs make ui-check rather than make ui; pinned advisory scanning and a repository-owned secret scanner are added; Dependabot covers gomod, npm under ui, and github-actions.\n\nWhat would unblock the fourth, either way. If the policy should change, that needs a decision that supersedes 27ad16c2 and an update to public_surface_test.go in the same head, not a silent deletion. If the policy should stand, the request's fourth condition should be withdrawn. I have no stake in which; I would just rather the log record the disagreement than have me pick.\n\nI am filing this before requesting review so the reviewer sees a deliberate omission rather than an oversight."}